.\" openi2pd: i2pdctl.1.
.\"
.\" Configures project configuration and integration.
.\"

.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt I2PDCTL 1
.Os openi2pd
.Sh NAME
.Nm i2pdctl
.Nd command-line client for the I2PControl service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a Perl 5 client for the local I2PControl JSON-RPC service.
It preserves the former project Python client's command names and output
semantics while using only core Perl modules and the system
.Xr openssl 1
binary for the self-signed HTTPS fallback.
The client never silently downgrades an HTTPS request to cleartext.
.Pp
The service is disabled by default and must be enabled in
.Pa i2pd.conf
before use.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm exec Op Fl j Ar method Ar parameters
Execute an I2PControl method with a JSON parameter object.
.Fl j
prints the raw JSON reply.
.It Cm raw_info Op Ar method ...
Retrieve raw JSON from
.Cm RouterInfo
or
.Cm ClientServicesInfo .
.It Cm info
Print a stable human-readable router, interface, and client-tunnel summary.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print command help and exit.
.It Fl j , Fl -json-output
With
.Cm exec ,
emit the raw JSON response.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev I2PCONTROL_URL
I2PControl URL, default
.Pa https://127.0.0.1:7650/ .
.It Ev I2PCONTROL_PASSWORD
I2PControl password, default
.Ql itoopie .
Change the router password before enabling the service.
.It Ev I2PDCTL_TLS_BACKEND
Set to
.Ql auto
or
.Ql openssl .
The latter forces the shell-free
.Xr openssl 1
s_client fallback for diagnostics and tests and still never uses cleartext.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print a router summary:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
i2pdctl info
.Ed
.Pp
Execute a method and print raw JSON:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
i2pdctl exec -j RouterInfo '{}'
.Ed
.Sh SECURITY
The default self-signed certificate is accepted by the compatibility client;
this is deliberate behavior for the local I2PControl endpoint.
Plain
.Li http://
URLs are accepted only when explicitly configured and send credentials in
cleartext; use the default HTTPS endpoint.
.Pp
The client bounds request and response bodies, validates the URL, ignores
SIGPIPE, and sanitizes server text before printing it to a terminal.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr i2pd 1 ,
.Xr i2pd-tui 1 ,
.Xr openssl 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
.An openi2pd
